SCOPE OF THIS GRANT

The license above covers the original authorship in this repository: the prose
of the reference and guides, its selection, arrangement and organization, the
provenance-tagging scheme, and the source code of the tools and scaffolds.

It asserts no claim over, and grants no rights in:

  * Facts about OS/2. API names, constants, structure layouts and offsets,
    error codes, ordinals and calling conventions are facts about a published
    interface. They are not the copyright of this project, and no exclusivity
    over them is claimed or implied.

  * Third-party expression. Short quoted passages and brief illustrative
    excerpts from IBM documentation and other sources appear throughout for
    identification, attribution and commentary, each marked at the point of
    use. They remain the property of their respective owners and are not
    licensed by this project.

  * Third-party software. No IBM, Arca Noae or other third-party software,
    headers, or toolchain is REDISTRIBUTED here — see sources.md for where to
    obtain those under their own terms. (Quoted documentation excerpts, as
    described immediately above, are the one exception and are not a
    redistribution of any of that software.)

BUILD-TIME DEPENDENCY — fpGUI (docview), GPLv2

tools/inf2txt is source-only for a reason. Our driver (inf2txt.pas) is MIT, but
tools/inf2txt/build.sh links it against fpGUI's docview units, and fpGUI
licenses per directory: its `framework` is modified-LGPL, but `docview` is
GPLv2, with no static-linking exception. A binary built by that script is
therefore a GPLv2 combined work. Building it for your own use is unrestricted;
redistributing the binary requires GPLv2 and corresponding source. No such
binary is distributed by this project. fpGUI is (c) the fpGUI Toolkit authors,
github.com/graemeg/fpGUI.

